  "question": {
    "text": "In a series&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LR</mi></math>&nbsp;circuit, power of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>&nbsp;is dissipated from a source of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The power factor of the circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. In order to bring the power factor to unity, a capacitor of value&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;is added in series to the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>. Taking the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math>, then value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "400",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math>. in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos&#981;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.8</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.8</mo></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.8</mo></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Power factor is unity</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>7500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2500</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>mF</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
